a. the provision of companions or volunteers for Children at the time of examination by investigators;
b. providing legal aid and psychological services;
c. involving members/investigators of the local police in efforts to prevent the occurrence of criminal acts committed by Children, Children as victims, and Children as witnesses;
d. realizing a restorative justice process for Children in conflict with the law; and
e. rehabilitation and social reintegration services.

